  "text": " There's this funeral director in New Zealand, and he discovered that 95% of the bodies coming in to his funeral were vaccinated within two weeks of their death. 95%. Have you heard that story? I have not heard that story, but what I have heard is that the vaccine is safe and effective and that it will slow the spread and the transmission and contraction, and it'll keep you safe from a serious illness or hospitalization or death. That's what I know about the vaccine. Yeah, and Jimmy. You have some story from some funeral director. An anecdote. Yeah, just an anecdote. That is just anecdotal. So go ahead though. Right, and here's the interesting thing, Jimmy. This blows people away. That I was only able to find negative anecdotes and I could never find a positive anecdote anywhere. I couldn't find a nursing home where the all-cause mortality went down. I couldn't find a funeral home where deaths went down. It's strange. It's really strange. So we're really confused while all the anecdotes we get are like, oh, all-cause mortality went up by two times or three times. I mean, I know a geriatric practice where they used to have 11 deaths per year every year. This year they had 33 and they looked at it and they kind of attributed it all to the vaccine. But hey, that's just their opinion. But you see, I can't find a place where the deaths went down.",
